prompt:
A real photograph of the beach at Kamakura, south of Tokyo, on a bright late-August afternoon, in a tall vertical picture, caught as it happens, as a friend standing on the sand would take it with a good phone camera. Taken with a 24 mm lens at standing eye height, looking down a little at two young women sitting on a towel and out across the beach to the sea and a small wooded island, everything in sharp focus. Strong summer sunlight and a hazy blue sky; the textures of real wet and dry sand, sea foam, water, terry cloth, straw, plastic, cotton and skin.

The first reference picture shows the young woman from the front, the second shows her from her side, the third shows her friend Yui, a Japanese woman of twenty-seven: the young woman's face, curly dark-brown hair and build, and Yui's face, short straight black bob and build, stay exactly as in them. Use them for the people only; here the young woman wears a plain white t-shirt, plain olive-green cotton shorts and a wide straw hat, and Yui a plain pale-yellow linen shirt, plain navy shorts and white sunglasses pushed up on her head.

Every surface in the picture is plain: the towels are plain single colours, the bottles of water are clear with plain blue caps, the beach umbrellas are plain single colours, the boats are plain white, and the bags are plain cloth. Each object stands clearly on its own, with a band of bare sand or bare water around it, so that the eye can tell at once where everything is.

The picture is built in three bands, from the bottom edge to the top edge.

THE FOREGROUND, along the bottom of the picture:
- the pale dry sand, with the shadows of footprints;
- a large plain orange beach towel spread on the sand; on it sit the young woman of the reference pictures and Yui of the third reference picture, side by side, seen whole, their bare feet in the sand; the young woman holds an ice-cream cone of white soft-serve, dripping down her fingers, high above her head at arm's length, laughing, while a large brown bird of prey swoops low over the towel towards it with its wings spread wide; Yui holds out a white paper napkin to her, laughing too;
- beside the towel: a canvas tote bag of plain beige, two clear bottles of water, a pair of white sneakers and a pair of sandals, a rolled-up blue towel, and a few small white shells and a flat grey stone on the sand.

THE BEACH, across the middle of the picture:
- the beach stretches away to the left and the right, dotted with a few beach umbrellas of plain blue, plain red and plain yellow, and people dressed for a hot day sitting under them;
- nearer the water, a small boy in a red cap digs in the wet sand with a yellow bucket and a spade, and a big black dog runs along the line of the waves;
- the line of the sea: small white waves breaking in long lines of foam on the wet sand.

THE SEA AND THE SKY, across the upper third of the picture:
- the wide blue-green sea; a white sailing boat with a white sail in the middle distance, and two surfers sitting on their boards further out;
- on the left, far out, a small rocky island covered in dark-green trees, with a slender white tower on top;
- on the right, the green hills of the coast;
- above, a hazy blue summer sky with a few white clouds, and three seabirds gliding high up.

The beach is sunny, wide and relaxed: between the objects and the people, the same bare sand, the same bare water and the same open sky.
